At the start of day \(n\), the snail is at a height of \(n-1\) feet. During day \(n\), it climbs 3 feet to reach a height of \((n-1) + 3 = n+2\) feet. To reach the top of the 30-foot wall, we set \(n+2 \geq 30\), which gives \(n \geq 28\). Thus, the snail reaches the top on day 28.

